{title: 126 - In the Bleak Midwinter}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #126 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 126}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]In the [Ab/Eb]bleak [Bb]midwinter [Bb7]Frosty [Db]wind [Cm]made [Db]moan;
[Eb]Earth stood hard as [Ab/Eb]iron, [Bb]Water [Fm]like a [Gm]stone;
[Ab]Snow had [Gm]fallen, [Bb7]snow [Eb]on snow, [Ab/Eb]Snow [Bb]on [Bb7]snow,
[Eb]In the [Ab/Eb]bleak [Bb]minwinter, [Db]Long [Eb]ago.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Angels [Ab/Eb]and [Bb]archangels [Bb7]May [Eb]have [Db]gathered there,
[Eb]Chrubim and [Ab/Eb]seraphim [Bb7]Thronged [Fm]the [Gm]air.
[Ab]But His [Gm]mother [Bb7]only [Eb]In her [Ab/Eb]maiden [Bb7]bliss,
[Eb]Worshiped [Bb]the [Fm/C]beloved [Db]With [Eb]a [G7/F]kiss.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]What [Ab/Eb]can [Bb]I [Bb7]give [Eb]Him, [Bb7]Poor [Eb]as [Db]I [Cm]am?
[Eb]If I were a [Ab/Eb]shepherd [Bb]I [Bb7]would [Fm]bring a [Gm]lamb;
[Ab]If I [Gm]were [Fm]a [Bb7]wise [Eb]man I would [Ab/Eb]do [Bb]my [Bb7]part;
[Eb]Yet what [Ab/Eb]can [Bb]I [Fm/C]give [Cm]Him? [Db]Give [Eb]my [G7/F]heart.
{end_of_verse}
